WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.977 --> 00:00:15.742
After seeing the freshly painted fence, Aunt Polly decided to let Tom play outdoors for the rest of

2
00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:16.402
the afternoon.

3
00:00:17.423 --> 00:00:21.665
The first thing Tom wanted to do was get revenge on Sid for telling Aunt Polly about his

4
00:00:21.705 --> 00:00:27.648
collar. So Tom waited by the fence and ambushed his half brother with balls made of dried-up mud.

5
00:00:28.832 --> 00:00:33.914
Before Aunt Polly could rush to Sid's rescue, Tom managed to hit him with six or seven balls.

6
00:00:34.654 --> 00:00:39.856
Sid screamed in fear and pain.Then Tom jumped over the fence and was gone.

7
00:00:41.917 --> 00:00:46.559
When Tom arrived at the town square a few minutes later, a group of boys was already there,

8
00:00:46.919 --> 00:00:48.240
ready to play army games.

9
00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:55.123
Tom and his best friend, Joe Harper, were appointed as generals, and they commanded their armies all afternoon.

10
00:00:57.203 --> 00:01:02.145
As the sun began to set, the boys counted their "dead" and "wounded," and it was determined that

11
00:01:02.206 --> 00:01:03.706
Tom had won a great battle.

12
00:01:04.807 --> 00:01:08.328
Joe and Tom shook hands and agreed to meet next Saturday for another battle.

13
00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:11.609
On his way home, Tom spied a new girl.

14
00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:16.972
He thought the new girl was lovely, with blue eyes and braided blond hair.

15
00:01:18.853 --> 00:01:22.954
At the sight of this new angel, the love Tom had pledged to a girl named Amy Lawrence

16
00:01:23.134 --> 00:01:24.115
instantly vanished.

17
00:01:24.875 --> 00:01:26.856
Tom soon began to show off for the new girl.

18
00:01:28.108 --> 00:01:32.052
He balanced a stick on his nose, and he walked up and down the street where they both

19
00:01:32.132 --> 00:01:38.677
lived. When the girl reached her house, she halted and looked over at Tom for only a second.

20
00:01:39.177 --> 00:01:40.739
But it was enough to encourage Tom.

21
00:01:41.519 --> 00:01:46.243
After she went inside, Tom lingered near her house, hoping to see her one more time.

22
00:01:46.844 --> 00:01:48.725
But the pretty new girl never reappeared.

23
00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:52.809
Still, Tom returned home in high spirits.

24
00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:58.044
His aunt scolded him for throwing mud balls at Sid, but Tom didn't care.

25
00:01:58.925 --> 00:02:02.466
When his aunt hit him for stealing sugar from the sugar bowl, Tom didn't care.

26
00:02:03.426 --> 00:02:07.627
He just smiled and said, "You never hit Sid when he takes sugar."

27
00:02:07.647 --> 00:02:12.068
"Sid doesn't torment me the way you do," she reminded him.

28
00:02:13.649 --> 00:02:16.149
That night Tom went to bed with the new girl on his mind.

29
00:02:17.169 --> 00:02:19.810
He was determined to devise a way to get her to notice him.

30
00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:24.271
The next morning Aunt Polly forced Tom to put on his Sunday suit for church.

31
00:02:25.232 --> 00:02:29.846
After a quick breakfast, she escorted Tom to church to make sure he attended Sunday school.

32
00:02:32.207 --> 00:02:38.010
The day's lesson consisted of memorizing five verses of the Bible, but Tom was having a problem concentrating.

33
00:02:39.111 --> 00:02:44.153
At last the lesson ended, and Tom and the other students had a fifteen-minute break before the church

34
00:02:44.193 --> 00:02:44.914
service began.

35
00:02:46.255 --> 00:02:50.977
Although Tom had not bothered to memorize the five verses, he had finally devised a plan to make

36
00:02:50.997 --> 00:02:52.378
the new girl interested in him.

37
00:02:53.959 --> 00:02:59.481
The other children had paid Tom to let them paint, so now his pockets overflowed with marbles, candies,

38
00:02:59.821 --> 00:03:01.001
fishhooks, and other goodies.

39
00:03:02.102 --> 00:03:05.522
Tom decided to use his new wealth to buy "verse recitation" tickets.

40
00:03:08.003 --> 00:03:11.804
These tickets were rewards for students who correctly recited verses from the Bible.

41
00:03:12.604 --> 00:03:17.066
For every two lines of verse correctly recited, students were given one blue ticket.

42
00:03:17.426 --> 00:03:22.167
Ten blue tickets equaled one red ticket; ten red tickets equaled one yellow ticket.

43
00:03:22.927 --> 00:03:25.408
For ten yellow tickets, a student could earn a Bible.

44
00:03:26.556 --> 00:03:29.178
A Bible for reciting two thousand lines of verse!

45
00:03:30.559 --> 00:03:34.461
Only older students were able to earn a Bible because it took years of saving tickets.

46
00:03:35.842 --> 00:03:39.044
Tom didn't want a Bible, but he did want to win the new girl's heart.

47
00:03:39.765 --> 00:03:43.647
To win her heart, he had decided that he must seem like a better person than the other

48
00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:47.790
boys. In church, the moment to impress the new girl finally came.

49
00:03:49.731 --> 00:03:54.034
First the minister asked all the smartest and most studious children how many tickets they had.

50
00:03:54.595 --> 00:03:56.236
None of them had enough for a Bible yet.

51
00:03:57.212 --> 00:03:59.676
"Does anyone have enough tickets for a Bible?"

52
00:04:00.016 --> 00:04:00.777
asked the minister.

53
00:04:01.639 --> 00:04:03.802
To the shock of everyone, Tom stood up.

54
00:04:04.302 --> 00:04:07.447
Then he proudly marched forward to bring his tickets to the minister.
